# Implementation Plan - Agent 5: CTO / Architecture Agent

Agent 5 (CTO / Technical Feasibility & Architecture Agent) is responsible for converting the validated innovation concept (from Agent 3) and team capabilities / tech stack choices (from Agent 4) into a production-grade, hackathon-time-aware system architecture.

---

## 1. User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Workflow Execution & Tech Stack Selection Flow**
> Agent 4 generates 2-3 ranked tech stack options (`TechStackOption[]`). The user can select a tech stack option via `POST /api/hackathons/:id/select-tech-stack`. Upon selection (or auto-selection default), Agent 5 (CTO) will trigger to generate the complete system architecture based on that chosen tech stack.

---

## 2. Proposed Changes

### Component 1: State & Schema Extensions (`src/graph/`)

#### [MODIFY] [state.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/graph/state.ts)
- Replace placeholder `ArchitectureResultSchema = z.record(z.unknown())` with strong Zod schemas:
  - `TechChoiceSchema`: Selected stack choices with rationale and team fit.
  - `ComponentSchema`: Frontend, Backend, AI Engine, Vector DB, Database, Cache, Background services.
  - `DataFlowStepSchema`: Step-by-step user interaction to backend, AI processing, database, and response flow.
  - `DatabaseModelSchema`: Collections, fields, types, indexes, and relationships.
  - `ApiContractSchema`: Endpoint path, HTTP method, request headers, body, response schema, and auth requirement.
  - `AiArchitectureSchema`: LLM model choices, prompts, agent tools, execution pipeline, and fallback policies.
  - `RagArchitectureSchema` (optional): Vector DB provider, embedding model, chunk size, overlap, retrieval topK, search filter.
  - `ExternalServiceSchema`: Third-party APIs, auth method, rate limits, fallback strategies.
  - `TechnicalRiskSchema`: Potential failure modes, impact, severity, and mitigation strategy.
  - `ImplementationPhaseSchema`: Phased hackathon timeline (e.g. Phase 1 Setup, Phase 2 Core AI, Phase 3 UI & Demo).
  - `TaskDependencySchema`: Breakdown of development tasks, dependencies, and role/member assignments.
  - `ArchitectureResultSchema`: Full structured payload matching `ArchitectureResult`.

---

### Component 2: CTO Agent Core Modules (`src/agents/cto/`)

#### [NEW] [cto.agent.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/agents/cto/cto.agent.ts)
- Main orchestrator function `runCTO(projectId, selectedIdea, teamAnalysis, hackathonParams)`
- Manages sequential sub-generator calls and aggregates into `ArchitectureResult`.

#### [NEW] [architectureGenerator.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/agents/cto/architectureGenerator.ts)
- Prompts Gemini LLM to generate `architectureOverview`, system `components`, `techStack`, `dataFlow`, `externalServices`.

#### [NEW] [schemaContractGenerator.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/agents/cto/schemaContractGenerator.ts)
- Generates detailed `databaseSchema` (MongoDB collections/fields) and `apiContracts` (REST endpoints).

#### [NEW] [aiRagArchitect.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/agents/cto/aiRagArchitect.ts)
- Generates `aiArchitecture` (prompts, tools, LLMs) and optional `ragArchitecture` (vector search setup).

#### [NEW] [implementationPlanner.ts](file:///d:/snist%20hackathon/src/agents/cto/implementationPlanner.ts)
- Generates `implementationPlan` (phased hackathon execution phases), `taskDependencies`, and `risks`.

